PRETABLE -- #545 adjudication repair, SECOND repair (the repair's own pass 2 found cells of the same space open),
written BEFORE its table runs.  NEVER AMENDED; corrections go to PRETABLE_Q2b.corrections.
Instrument before this repair: diff_footbridge.c md5 ff8f87b6 (491 rows).  dev_footbridge.c UNCHANGED (783c0c7f).
Pass 2 of the first repair: panel _scratchpad/panel_20260923_143458 (codex, grok, glm, kimi-k3 DO NOT SHIP; agy,
deepseek, minimax SHIP) + the Opus seat's MEASUREMENT (434 one-line variants, 153 green; _scratchpad/fbd5/q2r/opus/).
THIS IS THE THIRD CONSECUTIVE PASS TO FIND CELLS OF ONE SPACE, so the carrier's class-closure amendment governs: the
whole space enumerated from the handler's own inputs, closed in ONE diff, the contract naming what is not covered.

== THE SPACE, enumerated from the handler (the five arms + the dominating head) ==
  inputs: relative_addr (case label; the timer fold does not map onto the five addresses -- codex, grok, agy),
  writeflag {READ, WRITE} (the direction test), len {1,2,4}, idata (the legal Clear write reads it), irq_status,
  irq_enable, fiq_status, fiq_enable (read by the legal branches), the five latches (own: read by the decline; others:
  read by no branch of this arm).
  PARTITIONS THE BODIES TEST: direction; own latch {clear, set}; (irq_status & new enable) {0, nonzero} in the Clear
  write.  Everything else is a VALUE the bodies compute with, never test.

== WHAT WAS OPEN, measured (Opus results.tsv), and the row that closes it ==
  b_neg   `dir && !d->L` (any latch) -- legal x latch-SET, the VALUE channel: X7 checked only the announce count.
          Guest-visible at +0x184 (W180=0; line4+; R184 reads 0 instead of 0x10).       -> X10 (legal, every latch SET)
  fl_neg / or_L-later -- the cross-site latch ORDER: every multi-site sequence declined the sites in one fixed order.
          Host-visible (a later site's latch silences an earlier site's first decline).  -> X11 (20 ordered pairs)
  c_dir   `dir && len == 4` at +0x18c -- every legal write was len 4.  Guest-visible.      -> X12 (narrow Clear writes)
  idata   `dir && !(idata >> 8)` at +0x18c -- Clear data was only 0 / 0x70.  Guest-visible. -> X12 (all-ones data)
  bit_*   a condition keyed on a field BIT that no state sets (byte 1 of every field; bit 0; bits 18-29; byte 3 of the
          enables) -- grok (`irq_enable & 0x100`), agy (`irq_status & 1`), kimi (`irq_enable & 1`), glm
          (`fiq_enable & 0x100`), Opus bit_dir/bit_flag.                                -> a fourth state, ONES
          (0xffffffff in all four fields) in X6, X7, X9, X10 and X12: with all-zero, every single-bit condition on one
          field diverts in one of the two.
  lane    byte masks on a read value or a decline-body store (Opus lane_*): the ONES state makes every byte of every
          read value and every field non-zero.                                          -> ONES, as above

== CHANNEL: the new rows, the variant each is for, the observable that differs ==
  X10 legal len 1/2/4 read of <5 regs> (<4 states>, latches SET) returns its value (60) + IRQ Clear write 0x70
      (<4 states>, latches SET) clears and drives (4) -- 64 rows.  b_neg at every arm: the diverted read returns 0 or
      stale instead of the value; at A2 the diverted write does not clear (enable differs) and drives nothing.
  X11 first <decline i> after <decline j> latched: announced once -- 20 rows (seeded).  fl_neg / or_L-later /
      kimi's `!d->warned_irq_raw_w && !d->warned_fiq_raw_w`: the first decline of i announces 0 instead of 1.
  X12 IRQ Clear write 0x70 len 1/2 and 0xffffffff len 1/2/4 (<4 states>, latches clear) -- 20 rows.  c_dir: the
      narrow write is declined as a read (announce 1, enable unchanged, no drive); idata>>8: the all-ones write the same.
  ONES in X6 (+54), X7 (+35), X9 (+23): bit_* and lane_* -- the diverted access announces, or the masked value differs.
  PREDICTION, per Opus family, re-scored on the new instrument (all 434 of its variants, from its own one-hunk diffs):
    RED:   a_pos, a_neg, b_pos, b_neg, c_dir, c_flag, d_pos, d_neg, fl_pos, fl_neg, or_F, swap_flag, swap_body, bit_*,
           lane_*, or_L on a LATER latch, idata `!(idata>>8)`, dom idata-load width forms, !idata.
    GREEN (disclosed or equivalent, by family): e_dir and e_flag (a condition on one EXACT field value -- clause (e),
           the body never tests values); case labels added from outside and the widened timer fold (the ADDRESS axis --
           clause (e)); dir_eq (`writeflag != MEM_WRITE`: equivalent, writeflag has two values); or_L on the OWN latch
           (equivalent: sends an already-latched decline into a branch whose only effect is dead); idata `!= 0x20`
           (value-specific).  Expected green count: 20 + 20 + 5 + 2 + 5 + 4 + 1 = 57 of 434.
  FIX: 707 rows = 33 legacy (32 timer rows + IDENTITY) + 78 P + X1-X5 38 + X6 216 + X7 140 + X8 6 + X9 92 + X10 64 +
       X11 20 + X12 20.  Carried kills: every TABLE4 variant (49), Q1-Q5, W1, W2, T1, T2 keep every row they reddened.

== DISCLOSED, NOT ROWED (clause e) ==
  A condition on one exact field value (`d->irq_enable != 0x10`, `!= 0xdeadbeef`): the bodies test no values, and no
  finite set of states contains every value.  The ADDRESS axis: a case label added for another offset, or a widened
  timer fold, aliasing an address onto an arm.  Joint conditions over two fields beyond the four states, and over two
  latches beyond X11's pairs.  WIDE DATA on a declined write (data stays 0 / 0x70).  fiq_status has no writer in the
  product (grok, Opus), so every FIQ_STATUS / FIQ_RAW_STATUS value these rows seed is synthetic.  The guest reset-state
  reads: all seats that answered Q5 agree the offline rows carry the floor.
